WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
Identity comes first in
the chain, because policy,

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:06.513
devices and access all
target identity groups.

3
00:00:06.513 --> 00:00:12.175
The OU tree carried delegation, policy
scope and accountability in one structure.

4
00:00:12.175 --> 00:00:16.175
A flat cloud directory has none of
that until the program writes it down.

5
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:21.078
The book rebuilds it with four Microsoft
mechanisms bound into one model:

6
00:00:21.078 --> 00:00:26.062
attributes, dynamic groups, administrative
units and Conditional Access.

7
00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:31.429
Setting a user's attributes from the HR
record produces every downstream effect:

8
00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:37.037
group membership, delegated scope, policy
targeting, licenses and drift visibility.

9
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.100
One stamp, five outcomes.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.725
That only works if the
attributes are true.

11
00:00:41.725 --> 00:00:47.212
M-22-09 requires centralized identity
management for agency users.

12
00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:51.737
For the workforce, the authoritative
source is the HR system of record.

13
00:00:51.737 --> 00:00:56.137
HR owns who works for the agency,
where they sit and who they report to.

14
00:00:56.137 --> 00:01:01.088
A dynamic rule is only as trustworthy as
whoever can write the attribute it reads,

15
00:01:01.088 --> 00:01:04.561
so the help-desk and self-service
write paths are removed,

16
00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:06.925
and HR provisioning is the only writer.

17
00:01:06.925 --> 00:01:10.137
Then joiner, mover and
leaver run on their own.

18
00:01:10.137 --> 00:01:14.938
Tokens don't fix a wrong model; they
sign broken authorizations efficiently.

19
00:01:14.938 --> 00:01:18.254
So HR decides what the
authoritative attributes mean,

20
00:01:18.254 --> 00:01:21.201
and identity engineering
decides how they flow.

21
00:01:21.201 --> 00:01:24.225
Contractors need an authoritative
source of their own.

22
00:01:24.225 --> 00:01:28.680
Gate G1 requires the HR feed
working before any rollout.
